// halves of it are AccGetB / AccSetB below, which is what the accessor RUN is built
// from now that a property may carry at most one of each.
// The accessor RUN. Spelled `{ Accessor | PropVis }` it was an unbounded repetition, so
// psi/DuplicateAccessor.kt - `val a : Int` with TWO `get() = 0` bodies - parsed clean
// where Kotlin reports "Expecting a top level declaration" on the second. A property
// has at most ONE getter and at most ONE setter, in either order, and each of the two
// may be a body form (Getter/Setter) or a visibility-only one (`private set`).
// AccRunB is the same thing where at least one of the two must carry a BODY: it is what
